<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.6.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00952</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.6.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>f63a7fa9-2de3-4d16-811b-ed3ba3866b91</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="9c6931d4-9170-4176-bfd2-a8efa45fbed7" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
  <!--Q1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="2edfb5a6-2a2d-4b15-aba3-7fcdc835192b" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="True" data-solution-options="[&quot;True&quot;, &quot;False&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>This graph represents Andre’s distance from his bicycle as he walks in a park.</para>
      <para><figure><media alt="Graph of Andre’s distance from his bicycle, coordinate plane, origin &lt;span class="><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/2c0bfc03af451e800041ae81edee70d7127bd687"/></media></figure></para>
      <para>Decide whether the following statements are true or false.</para>
      <para>The graph has multiple horizontal intercepts.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! True</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Take a moment to think about what you learned in activit ies 4.6.2-4.6.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="7bfa27ce-1a34-45fc-ae81-c6b62d2c7364" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="True" data-solution-options="[&quot;True&quot;, &quot;False&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>A horizontal intercept of the graph represents the time when Andre was with his bike.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! True</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.6.2-4.6.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="36e11728-cc0e-4542-928c-89aa46d9aaa6" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="False" data-solution-options="[&quot;True&quot;, &quot;False&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>A maximum of the graph is the point (17,1)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.6.2-4.6.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="a404b2e6-3119-433d-a9a3-4392b006b4bb" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="3">
    <problem>
      <para>The graph represents the temperature, in degrees Fahrenheit, as a function of time. </para>
      <para> <figure><media alt="Function on coordinate plane."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/ad82b275cc44da777b992c3b1ffd859d0fb1ce42"/></media></figure></para>
      
        <para>At what hour in the afternoon does the maximum of the graph occur? Hint: Do not enter commas or spaces in your answer.</para>
      
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 3 p.m.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.6.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q3a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="50cd62ca-0eb7-4cb5-b9b1-1e205ac79cec" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="Starting height" data-solution-options="[&quot;Maximum height&quot;, &quot;Minimum height&quot;, &quot;Height staying the same&quot;, &quot;Starting height&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Match each feature of the situation with a corresponding statement in function notation.</para>
      <para><figure><media alt="Function on coordinate plane."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/3942afdc2f914a9eeb7201344ee56cc0a9ee3e7f"/></media></figure></para>
      <para>\(h(0)= 7\)</para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Starting height</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.6.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q3b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="4321f5b0-5277-42cb-8710-3a193370112f" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="Minimum height" data-solution-options="[&quot;Maximum height&quot;, &quot;Minimum height&quot;, &quot;Height staying the same&quot;, &quot;Starting height&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(h(1.5)\)</para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Minimum height</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.6.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q3c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="f8827eaa-9c81-457c-90b0-04d36a637ab7" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="Maximum height" data-solution-options="[&quot;Maximum height&quot;, &quot;Minimum height&quot;, &quot;Height staying the same&quot;, &quot;Starting height&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(h(4)\)</para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Maximum height</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.6.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q3d-->
  <exercise data-content-id="2d581c61-654a-4e65-b025-52d8746edc03" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="Height staying the same" data-solution-options="[&quot;Maximum height&quot;, &quot;Minimum height&quot;, &quot;Height staying the same&quot;, &quot;Starting height&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(h(t)=6\) for \(7 ≤t ≤8\)</para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Height staying the same</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.6.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q4a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="c322ec48-07c3-4c29-8e66-2583a3cf0c54" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="4">
    <problem>
      <para>The graph of \(f(x) =x^2\) is provided. </para>
      <para><figure><media alt="GRAPH OF THE PARENT FUNCTION Y EQUALS X SQUARED, WITH THE POINTS (1, 1), (2, 4), AND (3, 9) LABELED."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/8e96865debed8ceca9104cc834a822c518a3d995"/></media></figure></para>
      <para>What is \(f(2)\)?

          </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!  The value of \(f(x)\) when \(x\) is 2 or \(f(2) = 4\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.6.2-4.6.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q4b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="6b79e68e-ba10-4f57-bb67-d3dfe1fadd9f" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="1">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the value of \(f(1)\)?

          </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(f(1) = 1\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.6.2-4.6.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="871059dc-c8af-4dff-af07-3b73008398b5" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="3">
    <problem>
      <para>Shannon is running on a flat, rocky trail that eventually rises up a steep mountain. The graph below represents the total distance she covers with respect to time. 
          
          <figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/6ac1da9769751f767c0c0f55336f1a0ddce8b602"/></media></figure></para>
        <para>How many miles does Shannon run in 60 minutes? </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 3 miles</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.6.2-4.6.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> </div>
</div></section>
</content>
